roup":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"no trap of this class; full-context read","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:l00","model":null,"at":"2026-08-22","stale":false,"history":2},{"id":"trap-rhetorical-pivot","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"no trap of this class; full-context read","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:l00","model":null,"at":"2026-08-22","stale":false,"history":2},{"id":"trap-superlative","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"no trap of this class; full-context read","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:l00","model":null,"at":"2026-08-22","stale":false,"history":2},{"id":"trap-thesis-restatement","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"no trap of this class; full-context read","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:l00","model":null,"at":"2026-08-22","stale":false,"history":2},{"id":"trap-triples","group":"Voice","result":"fail","severity":"minor","notes":"flagged, not fixed. Proposed: 'Noble gases have R = empty, hence no open linking sites and no delocalisation.' TWO MATH FINDINGS, neither fixed inline. (1) THE BLOCK CONTRADICTS ITSELF ON THE NOBLE-GAS CONDITION. The classification table's last row reads '|R| = 2n^2 | Noble gas (no residual)' \u2014 i.e. the residual is FULL at capacity \u2014 while the 'Residual linking number' section three paragraphs later opens 'Noble gases have R = empty'. Those cannot both hold. The same split runs through lambda(R): the display says lambda(R) = 0 iff noble gas, but the closing sentence says metallic character 'weakens as lambda(R) approaches the closure threshold 2n^2', which treats lambda as growing toward the noble-gas end. Either lambda counts filled sites (then lambda = 2n^2 for a noble gas, contradicting the display) or it counts open ones (then the table's last row should be |R| = 0). The parent proposition's condition 1, |R| < 2n^2 for metallic character, sides with the table, so the 'R = empty' paragraph is the outlier. lambda is also introduced twice under two names, 'residual index' in Strategy and 'residual linking number' later, and collides with the partition lambda |- n used throughout the corpus. (2) THE 2n^2 CRITERION DOES NOT CHARACTERISE NOBLE GASES BEYOND NEON. Shell capacity 2n^2 gives 2, 8, 18, 32 for n = 1..4, but argon closes at 3s^2 3p^6 = 8 electrons in shell n = 3, not 18; krypton closes at 8 in n = 4, not 32. So '|R| = 2n^2 -> noble gas' is satisfied by He and Ne and by no other noble gas, and the halogen row '|R| = 2n^2 - 1' likewise works for F (8-1 = 7) and fails for Cl (18-1 = 17 against chlorine's 7 valence electrons). The rows encode the octet rule while the header says 2n^2. Lesser note: Cu sits in the 'approx half-filled d' row but is 3d^10 4s^1, a filled d-shell.","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:l00","model":null,"at":"2026-08-22","stale":false,"history":2},{"id":"voice-agent-speak","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"","reviewer":"script","by":"content/pipeline/qa-checkers-extended.ts","model":null,"at":"2026-08-09","stale":false,"history":1},{"id":"voice-ai-slop","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"Agentic heuristic check: pass.","reviewer":"agent","by":"one-voice-audit","model":null,"at":"2026-07-19","stale":false,"history":2},{"id":"voice-author-notes-pollution","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"","reviewer":"script","by":"content/pipeline/qa-checkers-extended.ts","model":null,"at":"2026-08-09","stale":false,"history":1},{"id":"voice-branch-jargon","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"[EXPIRED-NO-FIELD-HASH] No branch/audit working labels, agent status markers or first-person work narration found in the .md body or the .ts title.","reviewer":"agent","by":"local/one-voice-audit","model":null,"at":"2026-08-08","stale":true,"history":1},{"id":"voice-editorializing","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"","reviewer":"script","by":"content/pipeline/qa-checkers-voice.ts","model":nul